    "options": {
      "A": "Call the stopping-at-twenty list an unending sequence, because it uses number words.",
      "B": "The spoken list one, two, three, … works even if he scrambles the order of the words.",
      "C": "The ordered list one, two, three, … keeps going and stays usable for large piles; the finite list stops, and single marks become cumbersome.",
      "D": "Choose the darkest bead in the pile as the count."
